// CROWN control — the declared-!E cap must not over-reject: a pure lambda
// under `fn run(f) with !E` satisfies the negation and must be ACCEPTED.
// Guards the Hβ.infer.declared-row-vacuous fix against the twice-measured
// dead end (rejecting free tails at the gate: 646 false mismatches).
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn run(f) with !E = f()
fn good() = run(() => 42)
fn main() = good()
